\n  FROM ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HOLDING_001\n  WHERE investment_type = 'Equity'\n  GROUP BY investor_id\n)\nSELECT \n  ip.investor_id,\n  ip.investor_name\nFROM ATOM_ENTITY_INVESTOR_PROFILE_001 ip\nINNER JOIN ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HEALTH_001 ph \n  ON ip.investor_id = ph.investor_id\nINNER JOIN equity_holdings eh \n  ON ip.investor_id = eh.investor_id\nWHERE ip.risk_tolerance = 'Moderate'\n  AND ph.risk_score > 75\nGROUP BY ip.investor_id;"", ""generate_sql_reasoning"": ""The query uses a two-level aggregation pattern to avoid fanout from the one-to-many investor-to-holdings relationship. First, equity holdings are pre-filtered and aggregated to the investor_id level in a CTE. Then, the base investor profile table is inner joined with portfolio health data and the pre-aggregated equity holdings CTE. Filters are applied for moderate risk tolerance, risk score above 75, and equity investment type. The final result is grouped by investor_id to ensure unique investor records, projecting the required investor_id and investor_name fields."", ""generate_sql_parse_error"": """", ""generate_sql_raw_response_preview"": "" {\n  \""sql\"": \""WITH equity_holdings AS (\\n  SELECT investor_id\\n  FROM ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HOLDING_001\\n  WHERE investment_type = 'Equity'\\n  GROUP BY investor_id\\n)\\nSELECT \\n  ip.investor_id,\\n  ip.investor_name\\nFROM ATOM_ENTITY_INVESTOR_PROFILE_001 ip\\nINNER JOIN ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HEALTH_001 ph \\n  ON ip.investor_id = ph.investor_id\\nINNER JOIN equity_holdings eh \\n  ON ip.investor_id = eh.investor_id\\nWHERE ip.risk_tolerance = 'Moderate'\\n  AND ph.risk_score > 75\\nGROUP BY ip.investor_i"", ""pre_scan_validation_is_valid"": true, ""pre_scan_validation_reason"": ""Valid"", ""scan_status"": ""success"", ""scan_row_count"": 41, ""scan_error"": """", ""scan_error_type"": """", ""scan_raw_rows"": ""[{\""investor_id\"": \""INV-053\"", \""investor_name\"": \""Anita Iyer\""}, {\""investor_id\"": \""INV-058\"", \""investor_name\"": \""Mee