7871b488d8ce132ac8b0fe19f6f5a82b41806145ebcec8814c193f17e"", ""available_rules"": []}}, ""generated_sql"": ""WITH qualified_investors AS (\n  SELECT\n    ip.investor_id\n  FROM ATOM_ENTITY_INVESTOR_PROFILE_001 ip\n  INNER JOIN ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HEALTH_001 ph \n    ON ip.investor_id = ph.investor_id\n  INNER JOIN ATOM_ENTITY_SECTOR_ALLOCATION_001 sa \n    ON ip.investor_id = sa.investor_id\n  WHERE ip.risk_tolerance = 'Aggressive'\n    AND ph.liquidity_score < 50\n    AND sa.sector = 'Consumer Goods'\n    AND sa.allocation_pct > 0\n  GROUP BY ip.investor_id\n)\nSELECT\n  ip.investor_id,\n  ip.investor_name\nFROM ATOM_ENTITY_INVESTOR_PROFILE_001 ip\nINNER JOIN qualified_investors qi \n  ON ip.investor_id = qi.investor_id\nGROUP BY ip.investor_id, ip.investor_name"", ""generate_sql_reasoning"": ""The query implements a two-level aggregation pattern per the Query Spec. The CTE pre-aggregates by investor_id to identify distinct investors meeting all three filter conditions across the three tables through inner joins. The final query joins these qualified investors back to the profile table to project investor_id and investor_name, grouping by both fields to ensure unique entity representation as specified in final_group_by."", ""generate_sql_parse_error"": """", ""generate_sql_raw_response_preview"": "" ```json\n{\n  \""sql\"": \""WITH qualified_investors AS (\\n  SELECT\\n    ip.investor_id\\n  FROM ATOM_ENTITY_INVESTOR_PROFILE_001 ip\\n  INNER JOIN ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HEALTH_001 ph \\n    ON ip.investor_id = ph.investor_id\\n  INNER JOIN ATOM_ENTITY_SECTOR_ALLOCATION_001 sa \\n    ON ip.investor_id = sa.investor_id\\n  WHERE ip.risk_tolerance = 'Aggressive'\\n    AND ph.liquidity_score < 50\\n    AND sa.sector = 'Consumer Goods'\\n    AND sa.allocation_pct > 0\\n  GROUP BY ip.investor_id\\n)\\nSELECT\\n  ip.inve"", ""pre_scan_validation_is_valid"": true, ""pre_scan_validation_reason"": ""Valid"", ""scan_status"": ""success"", ""scan_row_count"": 13, ""scan_error"